{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SBvmUSZLPR9ZBbaNztg1T6","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# PRD: Production Checklist System\n     2→\n     3→**Version:** 1.2\n     4→**Date:** 2026-01-24\n     5→**Updated:** 2026-03-07\n     6→**Status:** Planning\n     7→\n     8→---\n     9→\n    10→## Changelog\n    11→\n    12→### v1.2 (2026-03-07)\n    13→- **CRITICAL FIX:** Corrected rundown segments Firebase path (was `production/rundown/segments/`, actual is `competitions/{compId}/rundown/segments`)\n    14→- Added `theme-configured` auto-validator (total auto-validated items: 14, total items: 75)\n    15→- Added fix links for `socket-connected` and `vm-online` (previously missing)\n    16→- Clarified contact \"auto-assist\" is NOT auto-validation — items stay manual type\n    17→- Clarified venue contacts (`venue-operations`, `scoring-operations`) are venue-scoped but stored under team key (known limitation)\n    18→- Clarified phase timeline labels are organizational only — no countdown/timezone logic\n    19→- Clarified checklist is not copied on competition duplication (starts blank)\n    20→- Added error boundary requirement\n    21→- Added Firebase security considerations note\n    22→- Added sidebar collapse behavior for Day Of phases\n    23→\n    24→### v1.1 (2026-03-06)\n    25→- Added checklist items definition document (74 curated items)\n    26→- Updated auto-validators to support N teams (up to 7) based on competition type\n    27→- Clarified: no `checkedBy` tracking in MVP\n    28→- Clarified: Firebase native offline support (no custom queuing)\n    29→- Clarified: socket/OBS validators show red when disconnected (expected pre-show)\n    30→- Clarified: custom VMs show red for VM health (no health check path)\n    31→- Clarified: checklist is pre-show only (no during-show or end-of-stream items)\n    32→- Clarified: site evaluation items deferred to Phase 3\n    33→- Updated item count from ~72 to 74\n    34→- Added reference to original CSV checklist\n    35→- Removed `checkedBy` from data model\n    36→- Updated related documents\n    37→\n    38→---\n    39→\n    40→## 1. Problem Statement\n    41→\n    42→Producers managing gymnastics broadcasts must track dozens of tasks across multiple days and systems:\n    43→\n    44→1. **No centralized checklist** - Tasks scattered across spreadsheets, emails, and memory\n    45→2. **Repeated manual work** - Same setup steps for recurring teams/venues\n    46→3. **No validation** - Producers can't verify system readiness before going live\n    47→4. **Lost institutional knowledge** - Contact info, site evaluations, lessons learned not captured\n    48→\n    49→Currently, producers use a 130+ item Google Sheets checklist that requires manual checking. There's no integration with the system to auto-validate technical items (VM online, OBS connected, rosters loaded) or to persist team/venue data across competitions.\n    50→\n    51→---\n    52→\n    53→## 2. Goals\n    54→\n    55→| Goal | Description |\n    56→|------|-------------|\n    57→| **Centralized Checklist** | Single page showing all pre-flight items with progress tracking |\n    58→| **Auto-Validation** | System automatically checks technical requirements (VM, OBS, Firebase data) |\n    59→| **Team Data Persistence** | Contacts, preferences carry over when working with same team again |\n    60→| **Venue Knowledge Base** | Site evaluations, camera positions, known issues stored per venue |\n    61→| **Template System** | Different checklists for dual meets vs championships |\n    62→\n    63→---\n    64→\n    65→## 3. User Stories\n    66→\n    67→### Story 1: Producer Reviews Pre-Flight Checklist\n    68→\n    69→**As a** Producer preparing for a competition\n    70→**I want to** see a comprehensive checklist of all required pre-show tasks\n    71→**So that** I don't miss any critical setup steps\n    72→\n    73→**Flow:**\n    74→1. Navigate to `/{compId}/checklist`\n    75→2. See overall progress: \"45/75 items complete (60%)\"\n    76→3. View items grouped by phase: Setup → Pre-Production → 2hr Before → 1hr Before\n    77→4. See auto-validated items (green checkmarks) for system-verifiable items\n    78→5. Manually check off completed tasks (communications, deliverables)\n    79→6. Add notes to specific items (e.g., camera op phone number)\n    80→\n    81→**Acceptance Criteria:**\n    82→- [ ] Checklist page accessible at `/{compId}/checklist`\n    83→- [ ] Progress bar shows overall completion percentage\n    84→- [ ] Phase tabs allow filtering by timeline\n    85→- [ ] Auto-validated items update in real-time\n    86→- [ ] Manual items persist to Firebase when checked\n    87→- [ ] Notes field available for each item\n    88→\n    89→---\n    90→\n    91→### Story 2: Producer Sees Auto-Validated Technical Items\n    92→\n    93→**As a** Producer checking system readiness\n    94→**I want** technical items to auto-validate based on system state\n    95→**So that** I don't have to manually verify things the system can check\n    96→\n    97→**Auto-validated items (14 total):**\n    98→- Event name configured → Check `competitionConfig.eventName`\n    99→- Meet date configured → Check `competitionConfig.meetDate`\n   100→- Venue configured → Check `competitionConfig.venue`\n   101→- Teams configured with logos → Check `config.team{N}Name` and `config.team{N}Logo` for all teams in comp type\n   102→- Rosters loaded → Check `teamData.team{N}.roster.length > 0` for all teams\n   103→- Headshots uploaded (>80%) → Count roster members with headshots, average across all teams\n   104→- Theme configured → Check `competitionConfig.meetTheme` exists (warning if not set, not error)\n   105→- VM assigned → Check `config.vmAddress` exists\n   106→- VM online → Ping VM status endpoint (shows red for custom VMs — no health check path)\n   107→- Socket connected → Check `ShowContext.connected`\n   108→- OBS connected → Check `OBSContext.obsConnected`\n   109→- Rundown created → Check `competitions/{compId}/rundown/segments` has items\n   110→- Segments named → Check no segments named \"New Segment\"\n   111→- Graphics assigned → Calculate percentage with `graphic.graphicId` (>= 80% = complete)\n   112→\n   113→**Notes:**\n   114→- Validators for teams, rosters, and headshots are **dynamic** — they check N teams based on competition type (2 for dual, 3 for tri, up to 7 for womens-7)\n   115→- Socket/OBS validators will show red when no one is actively running the show. This is expected pre-show behavior.\n   116→- Custom VMs will always show red for VM health since there's no health check path.\n   117→\n   118→**Acceptance Criteria:**\n   119→- [ ] Technical items show auto-validation status\n   120→- [ ] Green checkmark when condition met\n   121→- [ ] Amber warning for partial completion\n   122→- [ ] Red X when condition not met\n   123→- [ ] \"Fix\" link navigates to relevant configuration page\n   124→- [ ] Status updates in real-time without page refresh\n   125→\n   126→---\n   127→\n   128→### Story 3: Producer Manages Team Contacts\n   129→\n   130→**As a** Producer setting up communications\n   131→**I want to** store contact info for each team's key personnel\n   132→**So that** I don't have to re-collect this info for every competition\n   133→\n   134→**Flow:**\n   135→1. On checklist page, see \"Contacts\" panel for competition teams\n   136→2. View existing contacts: Head Coach, Assistant Coach, SID, Camera Op\n   137→3. Add new contact with name, role, phone, email\n   138→4. Contact auto-assists \"Camera op contact received\" checklist item (shows hint, stays manual)\n   139→5. Next competition with same team shows saved contacts\n   140→\n   141→**Contact Roles:**\n   142→- Head Coach\n   143→- Assistant Coach\n   144→- Sports Information Director (SID)\n   145→- Camera Operator (Primary)\n   146→- Camera Operator (Backup)\n   147→- Venue Operations (facility manager, A/V tech)\n   148→- Scoring Operations (meet director, scoring table contact)\n   149→\n   150→**Notes:**\n   151→- Contacts panel must handle **N teams** based on competition type (not just 2)\n   152→- Team keys are derived using `buildTeamKey(school, gender)` from `competitionUtils.js`\n   153→- **Known limitation:** \"Venue Operations\" and \"Scoring Operations\" contacts are stored under the team key, but they are venue-specific (a team's facility manager differs at home vs away). This is acceptable for MVP — most contacts are team-level. A venue contacts model (`teamsDatabase/venues/{venue-key}/contacts`) would be more accurate but is deferred to Phase 3 alongside site evaluations.\n   154→\n   155→**Acceptance Criteria:**\n   156→- [ ] Contacts panel shows on checklist page with tabs for all teams in competition\n   157→- [ ] Contacts stored at `teamsDatabase/contacts/{team-key}`\n   158→- [ ] Contacts persist across competitions for same team\n   159→- [ ] Click-to-call and click-to-email links work\n   160→- [ ] Contact existence auto-assists related checklist items (visual hint, item stays manual type)\n   161→\n   162→---\n   163→\n   164→### Story 4: Producer Tracks Progress Across Multiple Days\n   165→\n   166→**As a** Producer managing setup over several days\n   167→**I want** my checklist progress to persist\n   168→**So that** I can pick up where I left off\n   169→\n   170→**Timeline Phases:**\n   171→1. **Setup (5+ Days Out)** - Session creation, team config, initial communications\n   172→2. **Pre-Production (2-4 Days Out)** - Camera ops, YouTube, talent, rundown\n   173→3. **2hr Before** - VM, OBS, camera day-of setup, Virtius session\n   174→4. **1hr Before** - Discord, talent dry run, final checks\n   175→\n   176→**Flow:**\n   177→1. Day 1: Complete Setup phase items, check them off\n   178→2. Day 2: Return to checklist, Setup items still checked\n   179→3. Day 3: Work on Pre-Production items\n   180→4. Day of show: Focus on Day-Of items, all previous work preserved\n   181→\n   182→**Notes:**\n   183→- Checklist is **pre-show only**. No during-show or end-of-stream items.\n   184→- Firebase Realtime Database provides native offline persistence — no custom queuing needed.\n   185→- No `checkedBy` tracking. Items store only `checked` (boolean) and `checkedAt` (timestamp).\n   186→\n   187→**Acceptance Criteria:**\n   188→- [ ] Checklist state persists to Firebase\n   189→- [ ] Phase tabs show completion status (✓, ◐, ○)\n   190→- [ ] Timestamps stored for when items were checked\n   191→- [ ] \"Last updated\" shown on page\n   192→\n   193→---\n   194→\n   195→### Story 5: Producer Reviews Site Evaluation (Phase 3)\n   196→\n   197→**As a** Producer preparing for a competition at a known venue\n   198→**I want to** review the site evaluation and camera positions\n   199→**So that** I can plan camera setup efficiently\n   200→\n   201→**Flow:**\n   202→1. Navigate to `/{compId}/checklist` or dedicated site eval page\n   203→2. See venue info: name, address, capacity\n   204→3. View camera position photos and notes\n   205→4. Review known issues (e.g., \"subwoofer causes camera shake\")\n   206→5. See recommended internet settings\n   207→\n   208→**Notes:**\n   209→- Site evaluation checklist items (venue walk-through, camera angles, 360 video, etc.) are **deferred to Phase 3** and will be part of the venue database.\n   210→\n   211→**Acceptance Criteria (Phase 3):**\n   212→- [ ] Site evaluations stored at `teamsDatabase/venues/{venue-key}`\n   213→- [ ] Camera positions with photos, apparatus assignment, notes\n   214→- [ ] 360° venue photos accessible\n   215→- [ ] Known issues documented\n   216→- [ ] Internet speed and network info stored\n   217→\n   218→---\n   219→\n   220→### Story 6: Producer Uses Competition-Type Template (Phase 2)\n   221→\n   222→**As a** Producer setting up a championship event\n   223→**I want to** use a checklist template designed for multi-team events\n   224→**So that** I have the right items for this competition type\n   225→\n   226→**Template Types:**\n   227→- **Dual Meet Standard** - 2 teams, standard items\n   228→- **Tri/Quad Meet** - 3-4 teams, additional camera/graphics items\n   229→- **Championship Event** - 5-7 teams, extended communications, more camera ops\n   230→\n   231→**Flow:**\n   232→1. Create new competition as \"womens-quad\"\n   233→2. System suggests \"Quad Meet\" template\n   234→3. Producer accepts or chooses different template\n   235→4. Checklist pre-populated with template items\n   236→5. Producer can add/remove items for this specific competition\n   237→\n   238→**Acceptance Criteria (Phase 2):**\n   239→- [ ] Templates stored at `checklistTemplates/{template-id}`\n   240→- [ ] System suggests template based on `compType`\n   241→- [ ] Producer can override template selection\n   242→- [ ] Template items copied to competition-specific checklist\n   243→- [ ] Producer can customize after template applied\n   244→\n   245→---\n   246→\n   247→## 4. Phase Overview\n   248→\n   249→| Phase | Name | Priority | Goal |\n   250→|-------|------|----------|------|\n   251→| **1** | MVP Checklist | P0 | 75-item checklist, auto-validation, manual checkboxes |\n   252→| **1** | Team Contacts | P0 | Contacts database under teamsDatabase |\n   253→| **2** | Checklist Templates | P1 | Editable templates per competition type |\n   254→| **3** | Site Evaluations | P2 | Venue database with camera positions, photos |\n   255→| **3** | Camera Config Integration | P2 | Auto-generate camera config from site eval |\n   256→\n   257→---\n   258→\n   259→## 5. Success Criteria\n   260→\n   261→### Phase 1 (MVP) Complete When:\n   262→- [ ] Checklist page accessible at `/{compId}/checklist`\n   263→- [ ] 4 phases with 75 items displayed\n   264→- [ ] Auto-validated items (14) show real-time status\n   265→- [ ] Manual items (61) can be checked/unchecked\n   266→- [ ] Checklist state persists to Firebase\n   267→- [ ] Notes can be added to items\n   268→- [ ] Team contacts panel shows and edits contacts for all teams in competition\n   269→- [ ] Contacts persist at `teamsDatabase/contacts/{team-key}`\n   270→- [ ] \"Fix\" links navigate to relevant pages\n   271→- [ ] Checklist link accessible from ProducerView sidebar\n   272→\n   273→### Phase 2 Complete When:\n   274→- [ ] Template editor UI available\n   275→- [ ] Templates stored in Firebase\n   276→- [ ] Competition uses template on creation\n   277→- [ ] Producer can customize template items\n   278→\n   279→### Phase 3 Complete When:\n   280→- [ ] Site evaluation editor UI available\n   281→- [ ] Venue data stored at `teamsDatabase/venues/{venue-key}`\n   282→- [ ] Camera positions with photos stored\n   283→- [ ] Camera config auto-populated from site eval\n   284→\n   285→---\n   286→\n   287→## 6. Terminology\n   288→\n   289→| Term | Definition |\n   290→|------|------------|\n   291→| **Checklist** | Collection of pre-show items a producer must complete before going live |\n   292→| **Phase** | Timeline grouping of checklist items (Setup, Pre-Production, 2hr Before, 1hr Before) |\n   293→| **Category** | Logical grouping within a phase (Session Setup, Communications, etc.) |\n   294→| **Auto-validated Item** | Item whose completion is determined by system state (14 items) |\n   295→| **Manual Item** | Item checked off by producer manually (61 items) |\n   296→| **Auto-assisted Item** | Manual item that shows a visual hint when related data exists (e.g., contact info), but remains manually toggleable |\n   297→| **Team Key** | Unique identifier for a team, derived via `buildTeamKey(school, gender)` (e.g., \"west-chester-womens\") |\n   298→| **Venue Key** | Unique identifier for a venue (e.g., \"hollinger-fieldhouse\") |\n   299→| **Site Evaluation** | Documentation of venue layout, camera positions, technical specs (Phase 3) |\n   300→| **Template** | Predefined checklist that can be applied to new competitions (Phase 2) |\n   301→\n   302→---\n   303→\n   304→## 7. Data Sources\n   305→\n   306→**Original spreadsheet (130+ items):**\n   307→Source CSV: `docs/PRD-Production-Checklist/2026 Master_ Streaming Check List - Women - WCU - 12_5 - 7pm EST (4).csv`\n   308→\n   309→**Curated MVP (75 items):**\n   310→See [checklist-items-definition.md](./checklist-items-definition.md) for the complete item list with IDs, types, validators, and fix links.\n   311→\n   312→**Items excluded from MVP:**\n   313→- Site evaluation items (9 items) → Deferred to Phase 3\n   314→- During-show items (rotation changes, score updates) → Handled by show controller\n   315→- End-of-stream items (turn off streaming, shut down VM) → Not part of pre-show checklist\n   316→- Duplicate/redundant items from original spreadsheet\n   317→\n   318→---\n   319→\n   320→## 8. Related Documents\n   321→\n   322→| Document | Purpose |\n   323→|----------|---------|\n   324→| [checklist-items-definition.md](./checklist-items-definition.md) | Complete list of all 74 checklist items |\n   325→| [PLAN-Production-Checklist-2026-01-24.md](./PLAN-Production-Checklist-2026-01-24.md) | Technical architecture, data models, component design |\n   326→| [PLAN-Production-Checklist-Implementation.md](./PLAN-Production-Checklist-Implementation.md) | Task breakdown and progress tracking |\n   327→| [AUDIT-Production-Checklist.md](./AUDIT-Production-Checklist.md) | Audit findings and resolutions |\n   328→| [prompt-Production-Checklist.md](./prompt-Production-Checklist.md) | Implementation workflow for Claude loop |\n   329→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a68327e-d75f-4ecc-be6c-8aca5c4e0f1a","uuid":"aa254e4c-683a-471d-9deb-caffc49e6dbc","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Production-Checklist/PRD-Production-Checklist-2026-01-24.md","content":"# PRD: Production Checklist System\n\n**Version:** 1.2\n**Date:** 2026-01-24\n**Updated:** 2026-03-07\n**Status:** Planning\n\n---\n\n## Changelog\n\n### v1.2 (2026-03-07)\n- **CRITICAL FIX:** Corrected rundown segments Firebase path (was `production/rundown/segments/`, actual is `competitions/{compId}/rundown/segments`)\n- Added `theme-configured` auto-validator (total auto-validated items: 14, total items: 75)\n- Added fix links for `socket-connected` and `vm-online` (previously missing)\n- Clarified contact \"auto-assist\" is NOT auto-validation — items stay manual type\n- Clarified venue contacts (`venue-operations`, `scoring-operations`) are venue-scoped but stored under team key (known limitation)\n- Clarified phase timeline labels are organizational only — no countdown/timezone logic\n- Clarified checklist is not copied on competition duplication (starts blank)\n- Added error boundary requirement\n- Added Firebase security considerations note\n- Added sidebar collapse behavior for Day Of phases\n\n### v1.1 (2026-03-06)\n- Added checklist items definition document (74 curated items)\n- Updated auto-validators to support N teams (up to 7) based on competition type\n- Clarified: no `checkedBy` tracking in MVP\n- Clarified: Firebase native offline support (no custom queuing)\n- Clarified: socket/OBS validators show red when disconnected (expected pre-show)\n- Clarified: custom VMs show red for VM health (no health check path)\n- Clarified: checklist is pre-show only (no during-show or end-of-stream items)\n- Clarified: site evaluation items deferred to Phase 3\n- Updated item count from ~72 to 74\n- Added reference to original CSV checklist\n- Removed `checkedBy` from data model\n- Updated related documents\n\n---\n\n## 1. Problem Statement\n\nProducers managing gymnastics broadcasts must track dozens of tasks across multiple days and systems:\n\n1. **No centralized checklist** - Tasks scattered across spreadsheets, emails, and memory\n2. **Repeated manual work** - Same setup steps for recurring teams/venues\n3. **No validation** - Producers can't verify system readiness before going live\n4. **Lost institutional knowledge** - Contact info, site evaluations, lessons learned not captured\n\nCurrently, producers use a 130+ item Google Sheets checklist that requires manual checking. There's no integration with the system to auto-validate technical items (VM online, OBS connected, rosters loaded) or to persist team/venue data across competitions.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Goals\n\n| Goal | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| **Centralized Checklist** | Single page showing all pre-flight items with progress tracking |\n| **Auto-Validation** | System automatically checks technical requirements (VM, OBS, Firebase data) |\n| **Team Data Persistence** | Contacts, preferences carry over when working with same team again |\n| **Venue Knowledge Base** | Site evaluations, camera positions, known issues stored per venue |\n| **Template System** | Different checklists for dual meets vs championships |\n\n---\n\n## 3. User Stories\n\n### Story 1: Producer Reviews Pre-Flight Checklist\n\n**As a** Producer preparing for a competition\n**I want to** see a comprehensive checklist of all required pre-show tasks\n**So that** I don't miss any critical setup steps\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Navigate to `/{compId}/checklist`\n2. See overall progress: \"45/75 items complete (60%)\"\n3. View items grouped by phase: Setup → Pre-Production → 2hr Before → 1hr Before\n4. See auto-validated items (green checkmarks) for system-verifiable items\n5. Manually check off completed tasks (communications, deliverables)\n6. Add notes to specific items (e.g., camera op phone number)\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Checklist page accessible at `/{compId}/checklist`\n- [ ] Progress bar shows overall completion percentage\n- [ ] Phase tabs allow filtering by timeline\n- [ ] Auto-validated items update in real-time\n- [ ] Manual items persist to Firebase when checked\n- [ ] Notes field available for each item\n\n---\n\n### Story 2: Producer Sees Auto-Validated Technical Items\n\n**As a** Producer checking system readiness\n**I want** technical items to auto-validate based on system state\n**So that** I don't have to manually verify things the system can check\n\n**Auto-validated items (14 total):**\n- Event name configured → Check `competitionConfig.eventName`\n- Meet date configured → Check `competitionConfig.meetDate`\n- Venue configured → Check `competitionConfig.venue`\n- Teams configured with logos → Check `config.team{N}Name` and `config.team{N}Logo` for all teams in comp type\n- Rosters loaded → Check `teamData.team{N}.roster.length > 0` for all teams\n- Headshots uploaded (>80%) → Count roster members with headshots, average across all teams\n- Theme configured → Check `competitionConfig.meetTheme` exists (warning if not set, not error)\n- VM assigned → Check `config.vmAddress` exists\n- VM online → Ping VM status endpoint (shows red for custom VMs — no health check path)\n- Socket connected → Check `ShowContext.connected`\n- OBS connected → Check `OBSContext.obsConnected`\n- Rundown created → Check `competitions/{compId}/rundown/segments` has items\n- Segments named → Check no segments named \"New Segment\"\n- Graphics assigned → Calculate percentage with `graphic.graphicId` (>= 80% = complete)\n\n**Notes:**\n- Validators for teams, rosters, and headshots are **dynamic** — they check N teams based on competition type (2 for dual, 3 for tri, up to 7 for womens-7)\n- Socket/OBS validators will show red when no one is actively running the show. This is expected pre-show behavior.\n- Custom VMs will always show red for VM health since there's no health check path.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Technical items show auto-validation status\n- [ ] Green checkmark when condition met\n- [ ] Amber warning for partial completion\n- [ ] Red X when condition not met\n- [ ] \"Fix\" link navigates to relevant configuration page\n- [ ] Status updates in real-time without page refresh\n\n---\n\n### Story 3: Producer Manages Team Contacts\n\n**As a** Producer setting up communications\n**I want to** store contact info for each team's key personnel\n**So that** I don't have to re-collect this info for every competition\n\n**Flow:**\n1. On checklist page, see \"Contacts\" panel for competition teams\n2. View existing contacts: Head Coach, Assistant Coach, SID, Camera Op\n3. Add new contact with name, role, phone, email\n4. Contact auto-assists \"Camera op contact received\" checklist item (shows hint, stays manual)\n5. Next competition with same team shows saved contacts\n\n**Contact Roles:**\n- Head Coach\n- Assistant Coach\n- Sports Information Director (SID)\n- Camera Operator (Primary)\n- Camera Operator (Backup)\n- Venue Operations (facility manager, A/V tech)\n- Scoring Operations (meet director, scoring table contact)\n\n**Notes:**\n- Contacts panel must handle **N teams** based on competition type (not just 2)\n- Team keys are derived using `buildTeamKey(school, gender)` from `competitionUtils.js`\n- **Known limitation:** \"Venue Operations\" and \"Scoring Operations\" contacts are stored under the team key, but they are venue-specific (a team's facility manager differs at home vs away). This is acceptable for MVP — most contacts are team-level. A venue contacts model (`teamsDatabase/venues/{venue-key}/contacts`) would be more accurate but is deferred to Phase 3 alongside site evaluations.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Contacts panel shows on checklist page with tabs for all teams in competition\n- [ ] Contacts stored at `teamsDatabase/contacts/{team-key}`\n- [ ] Contacts persist across competitions for same team\n- [ ] Click-to-call and click-to-email links work\n- [ ] Contact existence auto-assists related checklist items (visual hint, item stays manual type)\n\n---\n\n### Story 4: Producer Tracks Progress Across Multiple Days\n\n**As a** Producer managing setup over several days\n**I want** my checklist progress to persist\n**So that** I can pick up where I left off\n\n**Timeline Phases:**\n1. **Setup (5+ Days Out)** - Session creation, team config, initial communications\n2. **Pre-Production (2-4 Days Out)** - Camera ops, YouTube, talent, rundown\n3. **2hr Before** - VM, OBS, camera day-of setup, Virtius session\n4. **1hr Before** - Discord, talent dry run, final checks\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Day 1: Complete Setup phase items, check them off\n2. Day 2: Return to checklist, Setup items still checked\n3. Day 3: Work on Pre-Production items\n4. Day of show: Focus on Day-Of items, all previous work preserved\n\n**Notes:**\n- Checklist is **pre-show only**. No during-show or end-of-stream items.\n- Firebase Realtime Database provides native offline persistence — no custom queuing needed.\n- No `checkedBy` tracking. Items store only `checked` (boolean) and `checkedAt` (timestamp).\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Checklist state persists to Firebase\n- [ ] Phase tabs show completion status (✓, ◐, ○)\n- [ ] Timestamps stored for when items were checked\n- [ ] \"Last updated\" shown on page\n\n---\n\n### Story 5: Producer Reviews Site Evaluation (Phase 3)\n\n**As a** Producer preparing for a competition at a known venue\n**I want to** review the site evaluation and camera positions\n**So that** I can plan camera setup efficiently\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Navigate to `/{compId}/checklist` or dedicated site eval page\n2. See venue info: name, address, capacity\n3. View camera position photos and notes\n4. Review known issues (e.g., \"subwoofer causes camera shake\")\n5. See recommended internet settings\n\n**Notes:**\n- Site evaluation checklist items (venue walk-through, camera angles, 360 video, etc.) are **deferred to Phase 3** and will be part of the venue database.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria (Phase 3):**\n- [ ] Site evaluations stored at `teamsDatabase/venues/{venue-key}`\n- [ ] Camera positions with photos, apparatus assignment, notes\n- [ ] 360° venue photos accessible\n- [ ] Known issues documented\n- [ ] Internet speed and network info stored\n\n---\n\n### Story 6: Producer Uses Competition-Type Template (Phase 2)\n\n**As a** Producer setting up a championship event\n**I want to** use a checklist template designed for multi-team events\n**So that** I have the right items for this competition type\n\n**Template Types:**\n- **Dual Meet Standard** - 2 teams, standard items\n- **Tri/Quad Meet** - 3-4 teams, additional camera/graphics items\n- **Championship Event** - 5-7 teams, extended communications, more camera ops\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Create new competition as \"womens-quad\"\n2. System suggests \"Quad Meet\" template\n3. Producer accepts or chooses different template\n4. Checklist pre-populated with template items\n5. Producer can add/remove items for this specific competition\n\n**Acceptance Criteria (Phase 2):**\n- [ ] Templates stored at `checklistTemplates/{template-id}`\n- [ ] System suggests template based on `compType`\n- [ ] Producer can override template selection\n- [ ] Template items copied to competition-specific checklist\n- [ ] Producer can customize after template applied\n\n---\n\n## 4. Phase Overview\n\n| Phase | Name | Priority | Goal |\n|-------|------|----------|------|\n| **1** | MVP Checklist | P0 | 75-item checklist, auto-validation, manual checkboxes |\n| **1** | Team Contacts | P0 | Contacts database under teamsDatabase |\n| **2** | Checklist Templates | P1 | Editable templates per competition type |\n| **3** | Site Evaluations | P2 | Venue database with camera positions, photos |\n| **3** | Camera Config Integration | P2 | Auto-generate camera config from site eval |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Success Criteria\n\n### Phase 1 (MVP) Complete When:\n- [ ] Checklist page accessible at `/{compId}/checklist`\n- [ ] 4 phases with 75 items displayed\n- [ ] Auto-validated items (14) show real-time status\n- [ ] Manual items (61) can be checked/unchecked\n- [ ] Checklist state persists to Firebase\n- [ ] Notes can be added to items\n- [ ] Team contacts panel shows and edits contacts for all teams in competition\n- [ ] Contacts persist at `teamsDatabase/contacts/{team-key}`\n- [ ] \"Fix\" links navigate to relevant pages\n- [ ] Checklist link accessible from ProducerView sidebar\n\n### Phase 2 Complete When:\n- [ ] Template editor UI available\n- [ ] Templates stored in Firebase\n- [ ] Competition uses template on creation\n- [ ] Producer can customize template items\n\n### Phase 3 Complete When:\n- [ ] Site evaluation editor UI available\n- [ ] Venue data stored at `teamsDatabase/venues/{venue-key}`\n- [ ] Camera positions with photos stored\n- [ ] Camera config auto-populated from site eval\n\n---\n\n## 6. Terminology\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|------|------------|\n| **Checklist** | Collection of pre-show items a producer must complete before going live |\n| **Phase** | Timeline grouping of checklist items (Setup, Pre-Production, 2hr Before, 1hr Before) |\n| **Category** | Logical grouping within a phase (Session Setup, Communications, etc.) |\n| **Auto-validated Item** | Item whose completion is determined by system state (14 items) |\n| **Manual Item** | Item checked off by producer manually (61 items) |\n| **Auto-assisted Item** | Manual item that shows a visual hint when related data exists (e.g., contact info), but remains manually toggleable |\n| **Team Key** | Unique identifier for a team, derived via `buildTeamKey(school, gender)` (e.g., \"west-chester-womens\") |\n| **Venue Key** | Unique identifier for a venue (e.g., \"hollinger-fieldhouse\") |\n| **Site Evaluation** | Documentation of venue layout, camera positions, technical specs (Phase 3) |\n| **Template** | Predefined checklist that can be applied to new competitions (Phase 2) |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Data Sources\n\n**Original spreadsheet (130+ items):**\nSource CSV: `docs/PRD-Production-Checklist/2026 Master_ Streaming Check List - Women - WCU - 12_5 - 7pm EST (4).csv`\n\n**Curated MVP (75 items):**\nSee [checklist-items-definition.md](./checklist-items-definition.md) for the complete item list with IDs, types, validators, and fix links.\n\n**Items excluded from MVP:**\n- Site evaluation items (9 items) → Deferred to Phase 3\n- During-show items (rotation changes, score updates) → Handled by show controller\n- End-of-stream items (turn off streaming, shut down VM) → Not part of pre-show checklist\n- Duplicate/redundant items from original spreadsheet\n\n---\n\n## 8. Related Documents\n\n| Document | Purpose |\n|----------|---------|\n| [checklist-items-definition.md](./checklist-items-definition.md) | Complete list of all 74 checklist items |\n| [PLAN-Production-Checklist-2026-01-24.md](./PLAN-Production-Checklist-2026-01-24.md) | Technical architecture, data models, component design |\n| [PLAN-Production-Checklist-Implementation.md](./PLAN-Production-Checklist-Implementation.md) | Task breakdown and progress tracking |\n| [AUDIT-Production-Checklist.md](./AUDIT-Production-Checklist.md) | Audit findings and resolutions |\n| [prompt-Production-Checklist.md](./prompt-Production-Checklist.md) | Implementation workflow for Claude loop |\n","numLines":329,"startLine":1,"totalLines":329}}}
